(* README *)

1 - Summary
    -------

    L001 formalizes the Aporetic Lemma as a constructive fixed-point,
    collapse, and obstruction layer over the M001 regulator substrate.

    The theorem does not assert classical excluded middle, does not refute
    excluded middle in Rocq, and does not introduce semantic truth,
    arithmetic provability, or modal machinery. Its mathematical core is a
    closure predicate on M001 formulas:

      C : Formula -> Prop

    The primitive closure equivalence is implication-induced:

      ClosureEquiv C A B =
        C (Imp A B) /\ C (Imp B A)

    The excluded-middle status used by L001 is internal to the closure:

      ClosureExcludedMiddle C =
        forall A, C A \/ C (formula_negation A)

    Full evaluation closure is stronger than the fixed-point argument needs.
    For a goal `G`, L001 isolates the goal-specific fragment:

      ClosureEvaluationFrameForGoal C Code ev G =
        exists c, forall x,
          ClosureEquiv C (ev c x) (Imp (ev x x) G)

    At `G := Bot`, this is the minimal self-referential power that produces a
    negation fixed point:

      exists B, NegationFixedPointFor C B

    where

      NegationFixedPointFor C B =
        ClosureEquiv C B (formula_negation B)

    If the same closure is closed under object-level modus ponens and supplies
    excluded-middle status at the diagonal formula, L001 derives `C Bot`.
    If the closure is also externally consistent, this becomes an obstruction
    to the decision principle. In its explicit undecidability form:

      closure_acceptance_undecidable_theorem

    states that no total Boolean classifier can decide the acceptance set of
    such a closure.

    The stable public import is:

      From L001 Require Import L001_95_API.


2 - Boundary
    --------

    M001 supplies syntax, axiom sets, regulator theories, checked derivability,
    symbolic regulators, and evaluation frames. L001 does not modify those
    layers. It reads an M001 regulator instance through:

      RegulatorClosure profile T Gamma A =
        regulator_theory_closure
          (regulator_theory_with_axiom_set profile T)
          Gamma A

    and

      RegulatorClosureEvaluationFrame profile T Gamma Code =
        RegulatorEvaluationFrame
          (regulator_theory_with_axiom_set profile T)
          Gamma Code

    Thus the M001 instance is explicitly generated from a
    `RegulatorLogicProfile`, an `AxiomSet`, and a `Context`.

    L001 depends on the public M001 API, not on M001 implementation internals.
    It uses M001's evaluation-closure interface as a fixed-point engine and
    then adds the closure-level excluded-middle and consistency hypotheses
    that turn the fixed point into an obstruction.

    The abstract layer also exposes a decomposition of the goal frame:

      ClosureDiagonalRep
      ClosureGoalImpRep
      ClosureImplicationCongruence

    together yield `ClosureEvaluationFrameForGoal`, provided the closure has
    `ClosureModusPonens`. The congruence condition is explicit because modus
    ponens alone does not make closure equivalence transitive.


3 - Proof Shape
    -----------

    Evaluation completeness names every unary behavior over codes up to
    closure equivalence. The weaker goal-frame form names only the one
    behavior needed for a chosen goal:

      x ↦ ev x x → G

    L001 obtains a code whose self-application yields a formula `B` satisfying:

      B ≃_C (B → G)

    With `G := Bot`, this becomes:

      B ≃_C formula_negation B

    The collapse is branch-based. If `C B`, then the implication
    `B → formula_negation B` yields `C (formula_negation B)`, and since
    `formula_negation B` is definitionally `Imp B Bot`, modus ponens yields
    `C Bot`.

    If `C (formula_negation B)`, then the converse implication
    `formula_negation B → B` yields `C B`, and the same final modus ponens
    yields `C Bot`.

    Consistency is not part of the fixed-point construction. It appears only
    at the obstruction boundary, where a hypothesis

      ClosureConsistent C = C Bot -> False

    converts the derived bottom formula into a contradiction.


4 - Obstruction Boundary
    --------------------

    L001_03__Aporetic_Obstruction.v separates collapse from obstruction.
    The collapse theorems in `L001_02__Aporetic_Lemma.v` derive an accepted
    bottom formula:

      C Bot

    The obstruction layer adds consistency:

      ClosureConsistent C = C Bot -> False

    and therefore obtains impossibility statements.

    At the generic closure level:

      ClosureConsistent C
      ClosureModusPonens C
      ClosureEvaluationFrame C Code
      ClosureExcludedMiddle C
        ==> False

    At the regulator instance:

      RegulatorClosureConsistent profile T Gamma
      RegulatorClosureEvaluationFrame profile T Gamma Code
      RegulatorClosureExcludedMiddle profile T Gamma
        ==> False

    A total regulator decision is stronger than regulator-level excluded
    middle, so it is obstructed under the same hypotheses.

    Equivalently, the acceptance set of `C` is undecidable:

      not exists d : Formula -> bool,
        (forall A, d A = true  -> C A) /\
        (forall A, d A = false -> C (formula_negation A))

    The yes-status branch is obstructed only when accepting the status formula
    provides a total regulator decision:

      RegulatorClosure profile T Gamma excluded_middle_status ->
      RegulatorDecision profile T Gamma

    The no branch is deliberately weaker. A refutation-only classifier does
    not collapse by itself. It becomes obstructive only in the presence of an
    explicit `RegulatorDoubleNegationBridge`, which converts accepted double
    negations into accepted formulas.


5 - Files
    -----

    L001_00__Premises.v

      Defines the generic closure vocabulary, closure decisions, evaluation
      frames, goal-frame decomposition, generic fixed-point lemmas, M001
      regulator-closure adapters, regulator decisions, status-branch
      readings, refutations, and the optional double-negation bridge.

    L001_02__Aporetic_Lemma.v

      Proves the Curry-style fixed-point factorization, the branch-collapse
      lemmas, the generic excluded-middle and decision collapses, and the
      M001 regulator specialization `aporetic_lemma`.

    L001_03__Aporetic_Obstruction.v

      Adds consistency as the obstruction boundary. It proves generic and
      regulator-specific impossibility theorems for excluded middle and total
      decisions, isolates the yes-status obstruction, records the optional
      double-negation bridge facts for the no branch, and exhibits the
      always-false refutation classifier as the refutation-only non-collapse
      witness.

    L001_95_API.v

      Exports the public closure aliases, named contract propositions, and
      contradiction-shaped API endpoints.

    L001_97_Artifacts.v

      Packages the certified contract endpoints and writes the assumption
      reports for `certified_aporetic_lemma_contract` and `aporetic_lemma_qed`;
      the compile wrapper guards both reports as constructive endpoints.


6 - Active Tree
    -----------

    M001_95_API
      -> L001_00__Premises
      -> L001_02__Aporetic_Lemma
      -> L001_03__Aporetic_Obstruction
      -> L001_95_API
      -> L001_97_Artifacts


